R: no hostbridge board at port B0H.
Add a hostbridge board to the machine, or set its port to B0.
$
R -- copy a file from the host into CP/M.  (1.3, 8086)

   R <hostfile> [cpmfile]
   R <pattern>

Examples
   R FOO.ASM            host FOO.ASM -> CP/M FOO.ASM
   R FOO.ASM B:BAR.ASM  ...to B:, under another name
   R SRC/FOO.ASM        out of a subdirectory of hostdir
   R *.ASM              every match

Files are copied BYTE FOR BYTE. The last CP/M record is padded with ^Z.
HDIR lists what is on the host. W copies the other way.
$R: $ -> $ records, $ bytes
$R: $
$R: a wildcard copies each file under its own name -- so a second name
   cannot mean anything. Drop it.
$R: the CP/M directory is full.
$R: the CP/M disk is full, or is read-only.
$R: a name is too long.
